  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scVI_n200 + multiprofile + transformer achieves the best result (0.653 acc), while image-only ResNet50 is very weak (0.208 acc). The multi-profile gain (~0.13) and encoder choice (scVI >> PCA >> scGPT) are well-established. The critical untested question is whether adding the weak image modality to the strong RNA signal via fusion provides any benefit or merely adds noise. This experiment (config_032) takes the proven best RNA backbone (scVI_n200, multiprofile, transformer) and adds ResNet50 image features via concat fusion, directly testing whether multimodal fusion can improve upon the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. It is the highest-information next step because the answer determines whether the entire multimodal search space (configs 016-051) is worth exploring further, or whether resources should be redirected to refining the RNA-only pipeline. Concat is chosen as the simpler, standard first fusion test before trying weighted variants."
}

